course: dictionary
lesson: 14210
title: Words for old windows
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Some words name small parts of buildings, and a mullion is one of them. «The mullion stood between the two panes of glass.» A mullion is not glass. The word «between» tells you it sits in the middle, dividing the window.
explain: The clues help you. Mullions are in old churches and Tudor houses, so the windows are old. «The old church had tall windows, each split by a stone mullion.» Split is a clue: the mullion cuts the window into parts.
explain: Try the swap check. Replace mullion with «bar» in the sentence: «The bar stood between the two panes of glass.» It still makes sense, so a mullion is an upright bar that divides a window.
fact: A mullion is a vertical (upright) bar that divides a window into two or more parts.
fact: «Mullion» means an upright bar of stone or wood in a window.
fact: Mullions are often found in old churches and Tudor houses.
fact: «Mullioned windows» are windows with mullions, and they often have many small panes of glass.
fact: In maths, mullions are often spaced equally: a window 3 m wide with 2 mullions has 3 equal lights.
exercise: «The old church had tall windows, each split by a stone mullion.» What is a mullion? | A picture made from coloured glass | A kind of church bell | A small wooden door | *A vertical bar that divides a window
exercise: A window 3 metres wide has 2 mullions, spaced equally. How many equal lights (parts of the window) are there? | 5 | 4 | *3 | 2
exercise: «Tudor houses have mullioned windows with many small panes.» Find and copy the word that means windows with bars dividing them. | *mullioned | houses | panes | small
test: In The Wind in the Willows, Toad Hall has ancient windows with mullions. What do the mullions do? | Make the window glow in the dark | Keep out the rain completely | Let the window open and close | *Divide the window into parts
test: A window has 3 mullions spaced equally. How many equal lights are there? | 3 | *4 | 6 | 2
exam: «The mullioned window of the castle-gaol was ancient and grand.» Which word means the upright bars that split the window? | *mullions | glass | grand | castle
